+# Private B2 installation, original getter and reserved Stop candidate
+
+This is an unexecuted source candidate for one finite owned laboratory. It is not
+an installer for a hosted database, a production Stop mechanism, a complete B2
+implementation, a source-recorder capability, or a native acceptance receipt.
+No SQL, Docker, provider, credential, repository or remote operation was performed
+when preparing these files. Parent/root source review precedes any native run.
+
+## Exact implemented boundary
+
+Only `installation`, `source_stop`, scoped original lookup and exact original replay
+are implemented. The other nine allocator/control kinds and all five downstream
+capture/admission/availability/closure/seal kinds explicitly refuse. Installation
+allocates the fourteen closed genesis identities plus its independent operation
+UUID, derives the original epoch/terminal views, and enters paused mode. The one
+reserved Stop uses its original preallocated action UUID and exact current head,
+then enters stopped mode without acquiring a source hold. There is no Resume,
+active fence, provider packet, abandoned reservation, reclamation or epoch rollover.
+A stale or uncertain Stop is never rebased or replaced. Capacity is not liveness.
+The finite fixture gives its two scopes distinct owner/run identities; legitimate
+shared owner/run associations across scopes are not implemented by this first
+slice and must not be claimed from its conservative global conflict refusal.
+
+Commands, Results, Receipts, Journal and Head follow the reviewed acyclic order.
+The native manifest is external to the original inputs and uses the reviewed
+policy/SQL/validator/constructor-catalog/capability-manifest hashes. Its completed
+hash may then appear in Policies/G/C. Neither the manifest nor catalog contains its
+own digest. All six wire limitations stay false. All fixture recorder/source policy
+pins are explicitly synthetic inert identities, not installed source packages.
+
+## Source and instance gold
+
+The fixture reads pinned regular held SQL/validator/policy bytes before its first
+role/schema write. It compiles the held validator bytes with an explicit `__file__`;
+it does not import a second unchecked pathname copy. The SQL fixes eight tables,
+sixteen functions and one deferred original-commit trigger in two new private
+namespaces. The fixture compares all eight table declarations against separately
+created source constructors in rollback-only reference namespaces, including native
+default/CHECK trees (source locations only normalized), FK endpoints, index shapes,
+owned row/array types, internal FK triggers and constructor-owned TOAST relations,
+attributes and indexes. It separately checks exact function signatures/bodies,
+flags/settings, effective access, owners, the one noninternal guard and role edges.
+Then it captures the instance's full catalog K and separately verifies canonical
+bytes/hash before populating immutable package inputs. K includes direct incoming
+and outgoing dependencies, shared owner/ACL dependencies and full parameter/default
+ACL inventories. A current hash alone does not authorize a package or source.
+
+This construction remains subject to peer/root review and actual native testing.
+In particular, source-derived catalog coverage must be accepted before calling its
+K a reviewed instance gold. No fixture-created principal or caller Boolean proves
+production authentication; socket-local test trust is not hosted TLS authentication.
+The NOLOGIN native owner can only SELECT private bootstrap anchors. Actors receive
+only schema USAGE and the two entry EXECUTE rights, with no private table/type or
+helper access. The actual session user OID/name/capabilities/scope are checked.
+Nullable capability membership must be literally true; NULL capability elements
+are refused by the table constructor. Genesis role/type/identity/package widths
+are checked before staging, including actual scope/installation IDs.
+
+## Charging and first-path evidence
+
+The preserved V3 policy has canonical SHA256
+`e5dca1d13839102fb1fdd261176393b73c770a95ab355eff74499169905bfba0`.
+The preserved arithmetic receipt gives the maximum distinct-seven-pin Stop reserve:
+76,533 conservative encoded logical bytes, nine new retained rows, ten final-key
+logical writes and twenty final logical index keys. One pending operation INSERT
+and its deferred UPDATE produce an upper eleven row-DML touches, twenty-three
+conservative declared-key touches and 144,142 encoded row-image bytes. The duplicate
+final-function observation is charged in both Receipt and operation metadata.
+Additional cumulative DML/key/encoded-image counters are derived from immutable
+originals; they are not extra uncharged Accounting fields.
+
+The first reachable Stop has four direct pins and six getter-closure pins. It is
+not the distinct-seven-pin state. All admitted first-path UUID/hash/family/role
+strings have closed fixed width; generated JSON wire quoting must still be checked
+against actual PostgreSQL cost output. Domain caps are independent: genesis8192,
+epoch2048 and terminal1024 UTF8 bytes; installation fields must fit the closed2048
+Command shape used in the reserve derivation. The full seven-pin maximum, all
+sixteen positions, remaining kinds, complete high-water charges and physical
+storage/resource tails remain later gates. A small passing Stop cannot close them.
+
+The initial test draft checks committed state/counts and attempts an independently
+observed table DML-statistics delta for its four-pin Stop. Statistics observation
+is bounded and may itself be refused/unobserved; no acceptance is inferred before
+execution. Logical keys are not PostgreSQL physical index tuples, HOT behavior,
+WAL, resident memory, disk or crash-durability quantities. Trusted fixture setup and
+per-test state arrangement are excluded from actor-operation DML counts; actor APIs
+never expose the fixture's reset path. Static bootstrap rows are counted in the
+initial retained-row baseline and their wire/metadata/key bytes are charged once
+on installation.
+
+## Transaction and getter limits
+
+The supported trusted writer uses READ COMMITTED, fixed local timeouts,
+`synchronous_commit=on`, one original submit SELECT and literal standalone COMMIT.
+The function return is provisional. The deferred trigger rejects early
+SET CONSTRAINTS, autocommit/other message forms, a second new operation in one
+transaction, wrong original writer, changed package/session and clock regression.
+It creates the completed Receipt/Journal/Head atomically. The fresh original getter
+rejects that writer's top-level xid8 and resolves authorization, the complete exact
+prefix, identities, original derived views, dependency associations and observed
+head in one STABLE parent SELECT snapshot. xid8 is transaction-origin metadata,
+never operation/epoch/cross-restore identity.
+
+These checks do not authenticate an arbitrary SQL client or prevent every legal
+setting change after an early trigger. The trusted executor must preserve settings
+through actual COMMIT. MVCC visibility is not a WAL flush, crash durability,
+calibrated UTC or final-visible freshness attestation. Timeout is never proof of
+rollback. An absent original is observed-absent-unknown, never terminal closure.
+A concurrent duplicate that first missed the original before waiting may stale-
+refuse after the winner commits; it must reconcile via the exact original getter,
+not claim that the waiter necessarily returned a replay or submit a new UUID.
+
+The selected response is one compact JSON text scalar plus one LF in psql `-A -t`.
+The8MiB complete response cap is a NEW finite fixture choice, not the preexisting
+provider PacketResult retention-cache8MiB cap or the independent A1 seal cap.
+There is no HTTP/hosted transport compatibility claim.
+
